  "question": {
    "text": "When resonance is produced in a series LCR circuit, then which of the following is not correct?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SGGO9",
      "text": "\nCurrent in the circuit is in phase with the applied voltage.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "kahar",
      "text": "\nInductive and capacitive reactances are equal.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IFcKP",
      "text": "\nIf $\\mathrm{R}$ is reduced, the voltage across capacitor will increase.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7Y8zq",
      "text": "\nImpedance of the circuit is maximum.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Impedance $(Z)$ of the series LCR circuit is\n$Z=\\sqrt{R^2+\\left(X_L-X_C\\right)^2}$\nAt resonance, $\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{L}}=\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{C}}$\nTherefore, $Z_{\\text {minimum }}=R$",
    "image": null
  },
